; ============================================================
; damaged.journal — write off broken/damaged inventory
; Move the broken quantity out of wherever it currently sits (a bin, the
; inbound dock, outbound staging, etc.) into an expense account, at the
; same per-unit cost it's carried at. This works from any pipeline stage —
; just point the negative posting at whichever account currently holds it.
;
; No VAT adjustment is needed here: input VAT was already reclaimed on
; purchase, and scrapping stock isn't a taxable supply in most
; jurisdictions. Check with your accountant if you're unsure, especially
; if the goods are destroyed rather than simply devalued.
; ============================================================

2026-02-10 Found 3 broken widgets during stock check in bin A1 ; order:123
    Expenses:Inventory Write-offs                            3 WIDGET @ 4.00 EUR
    Assets:Inventory:Warehouse:Bin:A1                       -3 WIDGET @ 4.00 EUR

2026-02-14 Found 1 broken gadget during stock check in bin B2 ; order:456
    Expenses:Inventory Write-offs                           1 GADGET @ 10.00 EUR
    Assets:Inventory:Warehouse:Bin:B2                      -1 GADGET @ 10.00 EUR
